1lck/Lithe-IDEA#753.body:
The macOS Monaco editor rendered on an opaque WebKit surface and only received a light/dark flag. Its display options also retained the bootstrap theme, so each configuration refresh could immediately overwrite the host-selected theme. As a result, switching the app color theme or enabling a workbench background left the editable area with Monaco's own surface instead of the surrounding workbench.

This change:

- derives the Monaco surface, text, cursor, selection, line, guide, and link colors from the active macOS `CodeEditorPalette`;
- includes the app color theme, appearance, and workbench background state in the editor configuration so an existing Monaco view refreshes when any of them changes;
- keeps the selected theme in the shared display options so option refreshes and newly created split editors cannot restore the bootstrap theme;
- makes both `WKWebView` and Monaco transparent when a workbench image is present, while retaining the native editor color for solid backgrounds;
- starts Monaco with a transparent bootstrap surface to avoid a hard-coded dark flash before the native configuration arrives;
- keeps shared syntax-token roles in `color-mappings.json` and records the native/theme ownership boundary in the Monaco architecture note;
- adds Swift coverage for native theme payloads and a real WebKit integration case for solid and transparent Monaco surfaces.

Local validation:

- `git diff --check`
- `node scripts/verify-editor-boundaries.mjs`
- `./scripts/verify-agent-notes.sh`
- `./scripts/verify-service-boundaries.sh`
- `./.agents/skills/write-stable-tests/scripts/verify-test-stability.sh`
- `bun test frontend/editor/src/source-text.test.ts`
- `bun macos/EditorFrontend/build.ts`
- `bun macos/Experiments/Monaco/build.ts frontend/editor/node_modules/monaco-editor --workbench-tests`

GitHub Actions passed the real macOS WebKit probe, Swift tests, Rust/Swift bridge tests, arm64 and x86_64 package builds, Windows checks, plugin checks, database checks, and all aggregate gates.

Closes #732
